1
00:04:39,130 --> 00:04:45,130
What if you had a universal remote...that controlled your universe?

2
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:24,260
Click is a comedy, drama, fantasy film directed by Frank Coraci.

3
00:13:57,391 --> 00:14:03,391
A married workaholic, Michael Newman doesn't have time for his wife and children, not if
he's to impress his ungrateful boss and earn a well-deserved promotion.

4
00:18:36,521 --> 00:18:42,521
So when he meets Morty, a loopy sales clerk, he gets the answer to his prayers: a magical remote that
allows him to bypass life's little distractions with increasingly hysterical results.

5
00:23:15,652 --> 00:23:21,652
Michael Newman, played by Adam Sandler.

6
00:27:54,782 --> 00:28:00,782
Donna Newman, played by Kate Beckinsale.

7
00:32:33,913 --> 00:32:39,913
Morty, played by Christopher Walken.

8
00:37:13,043 --> 00:37:19,043
Ammer, played by David Hasselhoff.

9
00:41:52,173 --> 00:41:58,173
Ted, played by Henry Winkler.

10
00:46:31,304 --> 00:46:37,304
Trudy, played by Julie Kavner.

11
00:51:10,434 --> 00:51:16,434
Click is a 2006 American fantasy comedy-drama film directed by Frank Coraci, written by Steve
Koren and Mark O'Keefe, both of whom produced with Jack Giarraputo, Neal H.

12
00:55:49,565 --> 00:55:55,565
Moritz, and Adam Sandler, who also starred in the lead role.

13
01:00:28,695 --> 01:00:34,695
The film co-stars Kate Beckinsale, Christopher Walken, Henry
Winkler, David Hasselhoff, Julie Kavner, and Sean Astin.

14
01:05:07,826 --> 01:05:13,826
Sandler plays Michael Newman, a workaholic family man and architect who acquires
a magical universal remote that enables him to control reality.

15
01:09:46,956 --> 01:09:52,956
The film is inspired by "The Magic Thread", a folk tale included in
The Book of Virtues: A Treasury of Great Moral Stories.

16
01:14:26,086 --> 01:14:32,086
Filming began in late 2005 and was finished by early 2006.

17
01:19:05,217 --> 01:19:11,217
Sony Pictures Releasing, under Columbia Pictures, released Click in the
United States on June 23, 2006, and received mixed reviews.

18
01:23:44,347 --> 01:23:50,347
It was made on a budget of $85 million and grossed $268.7 million.

19
01:28:23,478 --> 01:28:29,478
It was nominated for Best Makeup at the 79th Academy
Awards (it lost the award to Pan's Labyrinth).

20
01:33:02,608 --> 01:33:08,608
This makes Click the only Sandler-produced film to
be nominated for an Academy Award.

21
01:37:41,739 --> 01:37:47,739
The film explores themes of dying and death, regret,
workaholic, heart attack, architect.

22
01:42:20,869 --> 01:42:26,869
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
